'''Boroughs''' ({{langx|bl|delegación}} or ''distrito'') are the subdivisions of the [[Castejón|Castejón Metropolis]], the [[W:Capital city|capital city]] and a confederal entity of [[Balisca]]. As of {{CURRENT YEAR}}, there are 12 boroughs in Castejón. Each borough is headed by a borough council ({{lang|bl|{{W|cabildo}}}}), which makes it colloquially known as {{lang|es|alcaldía}}. The traditional "core" of Castejón comprises four boroughs: [[Ampurias]], [[Expansión]], [[Hisbanya]], and [[Sástago]].

Castejón is one of the 51 confederated entities of Balisca, alongside the other 43 [[Regions of Balisca|regions]] and six [[Communities of Balisca|communities]]. It was named {{lang|bl|Distrito Confederal}} (Confederal District) until 11 October 1920, when it was officially renamed the {{lang|bl|Metrópoli de Castejón}}. According to the [[2025 Baliscan census]], it is the [[Regions of Balisca|most populated]] region with {{nts|24479594}} inhabitants and the [[Regions of Balisca|seventh-smallest by land area]], spanning {{convert|7,950|km2|sqmi}}.
[[File:Castejón Metropolis in Balisca (zoom).svg|alt=Map of Balisca with Castejón Metropolis highlighted|left|thumb|293x293px|Map of Balisca with the Castejón Metropolis highlighted]]
Despite being defined as a "metropolis", it is not governed as a city but as a unit consisting of multiple subdivisions. As a result of the political reforms enacted in 1920, it is no longer designated as a confederal district and became a metropolitan region, a member entity of the Baliscan Confederation, the seat of the [[Confederal government of Balisca|confederal administration]], and the capital of Balisca. 

The largest borough by population is [[Llanito]], with 3,631,287 residents, while the smallest is [[Hisbanya]], with 456,927 residents. [[Ampurias]] is the most densely populated subdivision in Balisca. The largest borough by land area is [[Trinacria]], which spans {{convert|1,687.5|km2|sqmi|2|abbr=on|adj=ri2}}, and the smallest is [[Ampurias]], with {{convert|56.9|km2|sqmi|2|abbr=on|adj=ri2}}.

The most recent borough is [[Trinacria]], established in 1975 [[1975 Trinacria referendum|from]] the territory of [[Luzamontaña]] ([[Araucaria]]).

